senses.gloss:
अङ्ग 1. अङ्ग, ind. a particle implying at-
tention, assent or desire, and sometimes impatience;
it may be rendered by well; indeed, true; please;
rather; quick. It is often used (changed to अङ्गी,
q. v.) to form compound words, as अङ्गी-कर्तुम्, to
assent, promise; see under अङ्गी [cf. ἄγχι].

अङ्गति अङ्गति, इस्, m. (fr. rt. अग्), fire; a
Brāhman who maintains a sacred fire; Brahmā;
Viṣṇu.

अङ्गारिणी, f. a small fire-place; the region heated
by the sun, though no longer exposed to its rays;
N. of a creeper.

अङ्गारित, अस्, आ, अम्, charred, roasted, burnt;
(आ), f. a portable fire-place; a bud; N. of a creeper;
of a river; (अम्), n. the early blossom of the Kiṃśuka.
